Source data and required attribution
  The capacity records in paper_release_v1/inputs/final.csv, and all data derived from them,
  were built from the battery materials database of Huang and Cole, which is distributed under
  CC BY 4.0:

    Huang, S. & Cole, J. M. A database of battery materials auto-generated using
    ChemDataExtractor. Scientific Data 7, 260 (2020). https://doi.org/10.1038/s41597-020-00602-2
    Dataset: Figshare, https://doi.org/10.6084/m9.figshare.11888115.v2

  The records were filtered, cleaned and manually checked against the original journal articles
  (2025).  Capacities, compositions and test conditions were corrected where the articles differed
  from the database.  These changes are part of this work; the original database is unchanged and
  remains available from its own record.

  When you use or redistribute these data, cite both this repository and the Huang and Cole
  database above, and indicate any changes you make.

Other sources in revision_analyses/
  - revision_analyses/outputs/mp_table4/ contains records returned by the Materials Project API
    (CC BY 4.0).  Cite: Jain, A. et al. Commentary: The Materials Project: A materials genome
    approach to accelerating materials innovation. APL Materials 1, 011002 (2013),
    https://doi.org/10.1063/1.4812323
  - The tables in revision_analyses/literature/ hold values compiled from published articles, each
    with its page, table or figure reference.  revision_analyses/literature/candidate_refs.bib is
    bibliographic metadata returned by the Crossref API.

  No article text or article PDF is redistributed here.
